---
import BaseLayout from "../components/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms and Conditions"
  description="Terms and Conditions for using CortexFlow — content use, affiliate disclosure, warranties, and liability."
  canonicalPath="/terms/"
>
  <div class="prose-wrap">
    <section class="section">
      <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Terms and Conditions</p>
      <h1>Terms and Conditions</h1>
      <p style="color: var(--muted);">Last updated: September 30, 2026</p>

      <p>
        By accessing <a href="https://cortexflow.tech">cortexflow.tech</a>
        ("the Site"), you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, please
        don't use the Site.
      </p>

      <h2>1. What this site is</h2>
      <p>
        CortexFlow publishes hands-on tutorials, guides, and comparisons about
        AI agents, workflow automation, and chatbots. Everything here is
        educational content — not professional, legal, financial, or security
        advice.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Use the tutorials responsibly</h2>
      <p>
        Our guides include code, configurations, API keys handling, and
        infrastructure steps. Software changes fast: a tutorial that worked
        when published may need adjustments later. Always test in a safe
        environment before using anything in production, keep backups, and never
        paste secrets or credentials into places you don't control. You follow
        these guides at your own risk.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        All articles, diagrams, and original graphics on this Site are the
        property of CortexFlow unless stated otherwise. You're welcome to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>share links to our articles anywhere;</li>
        <li>quote short excerpts with clear attribution and a link back.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Please don't republish full articles, scrape the Site's content at
        scale, or present our work as your own.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Affiliate disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        Some links on this Site are affiliate links. If you buy through them,
        we may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. This helps keep the
        tutorials free. It doesn't influence our opinions — when a tool has
        sharp edges, we say so, affiliate or not.
      </p>

      <h2>5. External links</h2>
      <p>
        We link to third-party tools, docs, and communities for your
        convenience. We don't control those sites and aren't responsible for
        their content, accuracy, or practices.
      </p>

      <h2>6. No warranties</h2>
      <p>
        The Site and its content are provided "as is", without warranties of
        any kind — including accuracy, completeness, or fitness for a
        particular purpose. We may update, correct, or remove content at any
        time without notice.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, CortexFlow isn't liable for any
        damages arising from your use of (or inability to use) the Site or its
        content — including data loss, downtime, or costs from following a
        tutorial.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may revise these terms as the Site grows. Continued use of the Site
        after changes means you accept the updated terms. The "Last updated"
        date at the top always shows the current version.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms? Email us at
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.authorEmail}`}>{SITE.authorEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
